From ec2fb55df5e6e17964955fc055ed93b2f9a49dc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 01:44:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/65] perf(ecc): batched variable-time divsteps in
 Bernstein-Yang inverse

Evaluate each BATCH of safegcd divsteps several at a time (the variable-time
formulation of libsecp256k1's modinv64): count-trailing-zeros consumes a run
of g-even steps at once, and consecutive g <- (g + f)/2 steps collapse into a
single g <- g + w*f cancelling up to 4 (6 after a swap) low bits. Same divstep
sequence, matrix and delta as the one-step-per-iteration loop, without one
unpredictable branch per divstep. Shared by the Native5x64 and Wasm9x29 kernels.

Fq inversion 2.97 us -> 1.60 us on the 4-vCPU bench VM.
---
 .../ecc/fields/bernstein_yang_inverse.hpp     | 122 ++++++++++++------
 .../fields/bernstein_yang_inverse_wasm.hpp    |  30 +----
 2 files changed, 83 insertions(+), 69 deletions(-)

